# Circom Circuits

Inspect the circuit's templates, component wiring, inputs, outputs, includes,
tests, and TypeScript callers before editing.

Treat signal ordering, public/private visibility, field arithmetic, constraint
count, witness generation, and component names as compatibility-sensitive.

Do not replace constraints with assignments, remove constraints to make a test
pass, or assume mathematically equivalent code has equivalent circuit behavior.
Preserve malformed-input behavior and meaningful boundary cases.

Validate with the repository's CircomKit workflow and inspect generated output
when compilation, proving setup, verification keys, or verifier artifacts are
affected.
